From 0425349f10f4fa869597904e20d407df27a2cdef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 13:07:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 21/31] riscv: defconfig: a210: build the PCF8563 RTC into the
 kernel

The A210's only enabled RTC is the external NXP PCF8563 on i2c4 (the SoC
dw-apb-rtc is disabled in the board DT). i2c4 enumerates the chip fine -
the i2c client 4-0051 is present - but RTC_DRV_PCF8563 was built as a
module and the rootfs did not have it loadable, so nothing bound to the
chip: no /dev/rtc0, and the system clock only looked correct because NTP
had set it. Wall-clock time would not survive a reboot without network.

For a headless server, timekeeping across reboot is essential and must
not depend on module autoload or rootfs module staging. Build the driver
in, matching the board's drivers-built-in approach; the kernel then binds
it at boot and seeds the system clock from it via the default HCTOSYS.

Co-developed-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 arch/riscv/configs/a210_evb_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/configs/a210_evb_defconfig b/arch/riscv/configs/a210_evb_defconfig
index 655948c35fd01..e557444529077 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/configs/a210_evb_defconfig
+++ b/arch/riscv/configs/a210_evb_defconfig
@@ -415,7 +415,7 @@ CONFIG_NEW_LEDS=y
 CONFIG_LEDS_CLASS=y
 CONFIG_LEDS_GPIO=y
 CONFIG_RTC_CLASS=y
-CONFIG_RTC_DRV_PCF8563=m
+CONFIG_RTC_DRV_PCF8563=y
 CONFIG_RTC_DRV_XGENE=y
 CONFIG_DMADEVICES=y
 CONFIG_DW_AXI_DMAC=y
